# A finite self-spawning SIGCHLD trap, with job control left off.
#
# Two properties make this the sensitive probe for the direct dispatch path.
# Job control off is what steers waitchld to run the trap directly for the wait
# builtin, which is the call that never marks SIGCHLD in progress. And the
# children exit instantly rather than sleeping, so a reap lands inside the trap
# window often enough to matter -- a sleep-based workload puts the reaps
# outside it and almost never trips this.
#
# The trap starts another child on each of its first four firings, so the
# reaping continues while the trap is already running. Exactly ten firings are
# owed: six initial children plus four spawned by the trap.
n=0
trap 'printf "CHLD\n"; n=$((n+1)); if [ "$n" -le 4 ]; then (exit 0) & fi' CHLD
i=0
while [ "$i" -lt 6 ]; do (exit 0) & i=$((i+1)); done
wait
